{"availability":"available","full":"Daga01/beautiful-react-ui","name":"beautiful-react-ui","description":"🚀A collection of lightweight and easy-to-customise controlled React components 🚀","category":"Developer tools","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":7,"created":"2020-02-14T16:58:51Z","updated":"2020-02-12T20:41:52Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://beautifulinteractions.github.io/beautiful-react-ui/","topics":[],"demo":"https://beautifulinteractions.github.io/beautiful-react-ui/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:09.971Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:09.971Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:09.971Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T09:26:09.971Z","stars":0,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["In the last few year we've had a chance to test a good number of UI libraries, each with its own strengths and weaknesses, but none that matched our expectations in terms of ease of customization.","In fact, our attempt at customizing the style and behavior of the libraries we've tested would generally result in one or more of the following:","As a result, we've decided to develop a library putting ease of customization as our top priority, focusing on a solid, props-driven API and pure CSS."],"features":["an inordinate growth in the number of dependencies of our projects, often in the form of language transpilers / compilers causing our build process to grow in complexity beyond reason;","a struggle with components carelessly implemented as stateful components where a stateless approach would have resulted in a much better, more performant, more reusable product.","Small and lightweight","Fully written in old-school JS (although TS types are supported)","Based on Tailwindcss"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Daga01/beautiful-react-ui/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"15fff0244a226a0c9acc00bd7a52b984a5bce683d1bb5905b180177cd95967f8","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T09:26:10